+# War of Genesis — Bounded V2.7 Proof Adaptation
+
+Date: 2026-10-08. Owner: Codex. Authority: PLAN38 / PLAN41. Two representative pages: native hub.guides → guide.gear. No Market renderer, calculator, bespoke UI or extra representative page. Adaptation is a project method, not runtime config. Nine original technical authorities remain unique: Config, Page Inventory, Content, Facts (unused/unchanged), Media Manifest, media decisions, semantic theme values, search (disabled) and freshness/version semantics. This record cites their choices, not a copied contract.
+
+## Player and content decision
+
+Gear task: inspect the exact copy before choosing use/keep/sale check, with conditional steps and explicit stopping rules. Ordinary MDX/FAQ/manual links; no QuickAnswer/Steps/NextStep component. The old Gear page supplies editorial reasoning, not item mechanics. Existing recorded Steam policy §C supports exact Strife/Valor listing identities and Valor publisher-app attribution to 4891320 (accessed 2026-09-15). Class A/B app identity/platform facts do not prove Class C rarity/drop/upgrade/build mechanics. The checklist is Class D editorial method. No current rates/prices/profit/liquidity claim. New content publication/update is 2026-10-08, accessedAt remains 2026-09-15; no fresh verification or live model.
+
+## Visual decision
+
+Old WAR_OF_GENESIS_PHASE_5_POST_LAUNCH_QUALITY.md §§D/E records coal/slate/fog-silver/tarnished-brass values derived from Steam imagery as mood reference, with no copied artwork. Map only existing semantic token values; keep existing editorial type and comfortable spacing, use quieter existing interaction values. No new selector/token/engine. Generic style is auxiliary; masked identity depends on visible source-supported Strife/Valor and app-specific relationship. Actual reviewer recognition remains unproven and may fail. No inference from a branded OG or lack of BF image.
+
+## Media and journey decision
+
+Media Manifest unchanged/empty. Native directory promises one gear decision answer, not a catalog. Text can explain the bounded criteria and uncertainty without an image. An exact-item UI capture could help locate status/details and game-specific visual evidence could strengthen identity; neither has been obtained/reviewed for this proof. This no-media choice does not assert that the whole game needs no media. Decision Table keeps Human/visual review PENDING and records missing evidence; no waiver or fabricated PASS.
+
+## Review and evidence
+
+WoG exact eight inputs only; repaired common Core/components/routes/scripts/tests/CI/package/lock unchanged. No WS04B/WS07/AX/Safari/release acceptance. Actual outputs, browser observations and strict masked identification belong to the external current proof package and independent reviewer. Dedicated runtime Game Adaptation schema remains NONE.
